WEBVTT


00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.263
ripped by looxlike


00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.746
Chapter one.


00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:53.377
Sometimes, despite your
best efforts otherwise,


00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.546
life will give you lemons.


00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.026
When that happens,
you've got two choices, friend.


00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:10.399
You can wear a sour face
or make lemonade.


00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.450
I never should have
booked this city.


00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.043
Come on,
come on, come on.


00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.018
Finally!


00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.448
Huh?


00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.583
What, did you swim here?
Might as well have.


00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.684
This is exactly
why I tell you


00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.887
you gotta fly in
the night before.


00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.190
The less time I spend
in this city, the better.


00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.231
I know, I know, I know.
But you'll be enthused to know


00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.596
that I reamed
customer service.


00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.430
Your bag is gonna be
on the very next flight.


00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.696
But have no fear.


00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:27.206
There is a brand-new suit
waiting for you right here.


00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.433
Where'd you conjure
this up from?


00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.169
Well, rainmakers
make rain...


00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.608
Room key.
Voila.


00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.908
There's a gorgeous
latte-colored silk tie in there.


00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.039
I think you're gonna
love it. It's subtle...Latte?


00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.980
Okay, there's a red
one in there, too. Okay?


00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.417
Can you please
just look your best? Please, okay?


00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:44.820
Listen, all three Unicom
suits will fly in from New York


00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.485
day after tomorrow to see
if we can make a deal.


00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.152
All three of them?


00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:52.027
I'm Lane goddamned Marshall.


00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.530
Burke, for once in your life,
can you please take the elevator?


00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:59.902
See you.


00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.770
Coming to the seminar?
Okay.


00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.580
Okay. Big day. Big day.


00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.981
LANE: And don't forget
the DVDs and audio books


00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.822
available for purchase
all through the week


00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:57.260
at our booth down the hall.


00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.527
And now,
without further ado,


00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:05.401
the author of the bestseller
A Path Through Grief, my friend...


00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.770
No, my inspiration,
Burke Ryan.


00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.030
All right!


00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.660
Thanks, Lane. Wow!


00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.593
Whoo!


00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.139
You guys make
a guy feel good.


00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.937
I'm feeling okay.
How are you?


00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.673
ALL: A-Okay!


00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:51.080
Good.
Let me ask you a question.


00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.742
Any football fans
in the house?


00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:58.584
Certain college team not too
long ago lost their season opener.


00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.825
They're going nowhere fast.


00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:05.523
Then something happened.
Thank you.


00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:09.591
An event that changed everything
for their coach.


00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.796
The guy started
sleeping at the office,


00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:14.099
reinvented the playbook,
studied film.


00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:17.040
He was on the case 24-7.


00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:20.270
They went on to win
the national championship.


00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:26.280
Well, after all the fanfare
and the champagne, he traipsed on home,


00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:31.747
went upstairs,
went to his closet


00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:36.088
and removed his Browning
double-barreled shotgun,


00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:41.392
put it to his chin
and pulled the trigger.


00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:46.701
See, the event
that changed it all


00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.934
back at the beginning
of the season?


00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:53.476
His brother, his best friend in the world,
died of a heart attack.


00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:59.345
You might be able to get back
on the horse, do great things.


00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:02.786
Hell, you might even win
a national championship.


00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:06.655
But if you don't pay the piper,
he will come calling.


00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:13.125
I want to thank each
and every one of you


00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:17.693
for having the courage to really feel
the loss of loved ones.


00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.905
I know it's not easy.


00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.970
I've been there.


00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.406
How are you?
You okay?


00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.742
ALL: A-Okay!


00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.147
Good. All right. Say it one more time.
How are you?


00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:33.014
A-Okay!


00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.679
All right.
I'll see you in workshop.


00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.960
Perfect. Perfect.


00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:50.832
Good. Good. Great.


00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:53.662
Come on, loosen up a little bit.
You need a drink?


00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.933
Maybe you need a drink.
Waiter!


00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.942
Please, no drink.
Chapter 12.


00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:01.207
"Alcohol's no more a cure-all
than a Band-Aid on a bullet wound."


00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.306
All right. Now flash me
that sign of yours.


00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.653
Great. Give me that.


00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:15.284
Great. So, tell me,
what motivated the book?


00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:18.627
Uh, my wife died.


00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.062
I know.


00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.494
Why tell the whole world
about it?


00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:31.535
It was a way to coach myself
how to get through it.


00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:33.670
You know, I never intended for anyone
to actually read it,


00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:37.910
but my manager gave it to
a publisher and here I am.


00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:40.646
Yes, you are.
What happened?


00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.585
Uh...


00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:49.323
She was driving us
to dinner.


00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:52.194
Dog in the middle
of the road.


00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.929
Car swerved into a pole.


00:08:58.104 --> 00:08:59.901
She died instantly.


00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:09.073
It must have been awful.
I'm sorry.


00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:12.107
Appreciate it.


00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:16.147
Well, I think
I got what I needed.


00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:18.520
Great! Fantastic.
Nice to meet you, Jessica.


00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.320
Nice to meet you.


00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:21.985
You take care.


00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:23.050
Thanks.


00:09:24.797 --> 00:09:27.061
This way, guys.
Follow Burke.


00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.998
All right, everybody.


00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.763
Those of you who signed up for the
morning work group,


00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:32.269
you're in for a treat.


00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:33.362
Let's go! Let's go!


00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:35.430
Come out in the middle here.
Excuse us.


00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.836
Thank you.
Excuse us for a second.


00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:41.141
Sorry. Come on out here.


00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.316
Come on, everybody out.


00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:47.748
I want you to take
a moment and look around


00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.516
and tell me what you see
and what you hear.


00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.615
Okay? All right.


00:09:53.159 --> 00:09:54.285
Okay.


00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.384
Lorraine.


00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:57.224
Cars. Honking cars.


00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.820
Good. Natalie?


00:09:59.298 --> 00:10:00.390
Jackhammers.


00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:01.763
Anybody else?
MAN: Stoplights.


00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.062
Stoplights.
Cement.


00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:04.193
A homeless person.


00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.259
Trash.


00:10:05.338 --> 00:10:06.362
Middle fingers.


00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:07.599
Good. Excellent.


00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:11.040
Now remember that
and follow me.


00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:15.078
BURKE: All right. Now what
do you see? Lorraine?


00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:17.548
The ocean.


00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.042
Good.
Trees.


00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:21.875
The Space Needle.


00:10:21.954 --> 00:10:23.182
Skyscrapers.


00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:25.147
Mount Rainier.


00:10:25.224 --> 00:10:26.714
Rivers.


00:10:26.792 --> 00:10:28.259
Beautiful rivers.


00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:29.760
The sun.
Good.


00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:31.228
Naked hot-tubber.


00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:38.633
Wow. Little bit different
up here, isn't it?


00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:41.366
And yet, it's the same.


00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:44.634
We haven't gone anywhere.


00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:49.012
We're just
looking at things from
a new perspective.


00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:56.183
Inside of each of you, there are sirens,
honking horns and gridlock,


00:10:58.691 --> 00:11:02.752
but there's also this.


00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.525
We just have to do the work


00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.034
and climb the stairs
to find it.


00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.998
You have the reporter at noon and
I think you're gonna like her a lot.


00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:15.540
Look, I don't
really give a rat's ass


00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:17.007
what your
cancellation policy is.


00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.566
I am leaving and
I want my money back.


00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:20.168
Sir, it's not that simple.
I'll be right back.


00:11:20.246 --> 00:11:21.838
Our cancellation
policy clearly...


00:11:21.914 --> 00:11:23.677
Hi. Becky? What seems to be
the trouble here?


00:11:23.749 --> 00:11:26.718
Mr. Ryan, this gentleman
is refusing to adhere...


00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:28.913
Thank you.
Hi. I'm Burke.


00:11:29.689 --> 00:11:30.747
You are?


00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:31.949
Walter Mayfield.


00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:33.013
Walter. Where you from?


00:11:33.092 --> 00:11:34.889
Billings. Drove out
from Billings.


00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.621
Montana.
That's quite a drive.


00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:40.188
Yeah. Look, I don't think
this thing is for me, okay?


00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:42.200
Okay. You mind
if I ask why?


00:11:42.268 --> 00:11:46.466
Well, frankly, my sister talked me
into it, and the...


00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:49.099
You know, the whole...
And the feelings...


00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:51.006
I understand.
I understand.


00:11:51.077 --> 00:11:53.238
Can I ask you,
why did your sister think


00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:55.780
it was so important
for you to come here?


00:11:58.651 --> 00:11:59.845
My son.


00:11:59.919 --> 00:12:01.853
And what's his name?
Stephen.


00:12:01.921 --> 00:12:03.980
And when did he...
Does it really matter?


00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:06.786
It matters to me, Walter.
I'd like to hear.


00:12:12.164 --> 00:12:14.132
Do you have a picture?


00:12:32.485 --> 00:12:33.884
I'm sorry.


00:12:36.989 --> 00:12:38.752
Walter, I know how you feel.
I've been there.


00:12:40.159 --> 00:12:42.821
My wife died.
Three years ago.


00:12:44.864 --> 00:12:46.354
I want you to know that
you've taken the first step


00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:49.367
just by walking through these doors,
and something inside you,


00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:53.064
whether you know it or not,
made you drive all this way.


00:12:55.141 --> 00:12:58.304
If you want to leave,
we'll honor your request.


00:12:59.311 --> 00:13:01.074
I hope you don't.


00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:07.279
Thanks, Becky.
Think about it.


00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.052
Chapter two.
Happiness is a state of mind


00:13:19.265 --> 00:13:21.893
and, like all things,
it takes practice.


00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:26.199
Devote five minutes a day
to smiling, just smiling,


00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.175
and after a while
it'll come naturally.


00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:55.065
Sorry. I didn't mean to...


00:14:10.316 --> 00:14:12.409
Hey, you forgot your pen!


00:14:26.599 --> 00:14:28.430
Quidnunc? Quidnunc?


00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:43.072
What can I get you?


00:14:43.148 --> 00:14:47.642
I would like another Seven-and-Seven,
and a tomato juice


00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:48.709
for my virtuous friend here.


00:14:48.787 --> 00:14:49.913
Tomato juice.


00:14:49.989 --> 00:14:51.616
Thank you.


00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:54.591
So, as far as
Unicom knows,


00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.061
I'm a hair away from signing a deal
with Time Warner. Okay?


00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.189
I'm expecting the offer
by lunchtime tomorrow.


00:15:00.266 --> 00:15:05.670
That means TV, radio, publishing.
All of it.


00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:09.641
Are you as hot for me right now
as I am hot for me right now?


00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:10.732
So hot.


00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:12.003
And check it.


00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:16.111
Ted Vernon, the CEO himself, is gonna
fly in for the end of the seminar.


00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:19.344
My guess, a little warm and fuzzy
contract-inking party.


00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:20.817
Who knows?


00:15:20.886 --> 00:15:22.353
Your drinks, gentlemen.


00:15:22.922 --> 00:15:24.082
Thank you.


00:15:28.193 --> 00:15:29.683
It's a long way
from booking you gigs


00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:32.287
writing columns
for Psychology Today, huh?


00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:41.029
I'll get you a Learjet.


00:15:41.807 --> 00:15:42.831
You like Learjets?


00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:44.136
Lane.


00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.674
Come on. You know
that's not why I wrote it.


00:15:49.515 --> 00:15:52.973
You do know that you're helping people,
right, man?


00:15:57.122 --> 00:15:58.987
This is your moment.


00:15:59.758 --> 00:16:02.784
You have to give yourself permission
to enjoy it, brother.


00:16:03.562 --> 00:16:06.122
Come on, man.
Live a little.


00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:07.990
Yeah.


00:16:08.067 --> 00:16:09.091
Yeah.


00:16:15.741 --> 00:16:16.901
What?


00:16:34.393 --> 00:16:35.951
You're right.


00:16:50.476 --> 00:16:52.341
Excuse me. I'm sorry.


00:16:52.945 --> 00:16:56.642
Hi. Do you remember me?
From the hallway upstairs?


00:16:56.715 --> 00:16:58.615
You dropped your pen.


00:17:00.452 --> 00:17:01.578
Um...


00:17:01.987 --> 00:17:04.751
Would you like to
have a cup of coffee?


00:17:09.895 --> 00:17:10.884
Ah.


00:17:11.296 --> 00:17:12.558
Right. Um...


00:17:13.899 --> 00:17:17.266
Well, we could bring him along
if you want. Double your pleasure.


00:17:24.543 --> 00:17:27.341
I'm sorry.
I... I... You...


00:17:32.785 --> 00:17:33.979
See you, Ricky.


00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:35.179
Later, Eloise.


00:17:56.642 --> 00:17:59.440
Hey, baby. What's this?
Delivery.


00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:01.110
Wow.
I was in the
neighborhood,


00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.545
so I figured
I'd bring you lunch


00:18:02.614 --> 00:18:04.639
'cause I knew you'd
be working so hard.


00:18:04.716 --> 00:18:05.705
Wow, you didn't
have to do that.


00:18:05.784 --> 00:18:07.183
Polished up, ready to go.


00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:08.276
Hey, Eloise.


00:18:08.353 --> 00:18:09.445
Hi, lan.


00:18:09.988 --> 00:18:11.717
How's your boss
treating you today?


00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:13.485
Oh, he's all right.


00:18:13.559 --> 00:18:16.790
The lead singer of the Stereo Kings
trashed his Les Paul.


00:18:16.862 --> 00:18:19.990
Look at that fretboard, man.
As good as new.


00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:21.259
Make sure
he signs for it.


00:18:21.333 --> 00:18:22.664
No problem.


00:18:23.869 --> 00:18:25.097
Did you have company?


00:18:26.738 --> 00:18:27.727
Um...


00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:31.332
Yeah. I told you Frank and I were
working last night.


00:18:32.344 --> 00:18:33.971
Frank wears lipstick?


00:18:35.848 --> 00:18:37.611
Hey, listen. EI, it's not
what you think.


00:18:37.683 --> 00:18:39.014
It's business.
Totally platonic.


00:18:39.084 --> 00:18:40.676
You know what? You used
that one last time.


00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:43.448
No, she's got ties
to Sony. Hey!


00:18:43.522 --> 00:18:46.047
Listen to me. You gotta listen
to me. Eloise!


00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:47.956
I don't want to hear it.


00:20:03.735 --> 00:20:04.963
How you doing today?


00:20:05.037 --> 00:20:06.470
Pretty good, thanks.


00:20:06.772 --> 00:20:08.467
All right. Okay.


00:20:10.709 --> 00:20:11.733
What's your name?


00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:12.834
Alberto.


00:20:13.779 --> 00:20:15.178
See you at workshop,
okay? Goodbye.


00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:16.805
Mr. Ryan.


00:20:17.082 --> 00:20:19.312
You are something.
Yes, sir.


00:20:20.419 --> 00:20:24.480
Say, would you mind signing that to
"Donald and Shirley," please?


00:20:25.357 --> 00:20:26.949
There you go.


00:20:27.025 --> 00:20:28.322
Say, do you mind
if I share?


00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.749
Share?


00:20:29.828 --> 00:20:32.490
Yeah. See, there's
this fellow in his 60s


00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:36.159
and he thinks he's just gonna,
you know, sail through his retirement.


00:20:36.235 --> 00:20:40.103
But then one day, three years and
13 days ago,


00:20:40.172 --> 00:20:42.367
his daughter dies.


00:20:43.342 --> 00:20:46.675
And the truth is he hasn't been
doing very well.


00:20:47.446 --> 00:20:51.075
He doesn't sleep much,
and he and his wife, well...


00:20:52.484 --> 00:20:54.076
You can understand.


00:20:54.152 --> 00:20:56.780
But his daughter's husband,


00:20:56.855 --> 00:20:58.117
well, he doesn't
seem to be having


00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.124
any of these kinds
of problems. No.


00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:05.522
She was crushed to death in a car crash,
but he, well...


00:21:07.432 --> 00:21:11.960
He's making lemonade out of lemons.
Isn't that how it goes?


00:21:20.012 --> 00:21:22.606
When are you gonna
stop lying, son?


00:21:26.785 --> 00:21:28.218
Hypocrite.


00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:36.290
Burke, I am so sorry.


00:21:37.529 --> 00:21:39.861
God. The balls on him!


00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:41.159
I'm fine.


00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:44.424
Who does he think he is?


