00:40:32.496 --> 00:40:34.225
Come on, Walter!


00:40:37.935 --> 00:40:39.334
Here we go.


00:40:39.403 --> 00:40:41.371
Come on, Walter!


00:40:42.239 --> 00:40:43.536
Come on!


00:40:44.074 --> 00:40:45.336
Walter.


00:40:46.310 --> 00:40:47.868
It's okay. It's okay.


00:40:47.945 --> 00:40:51.108
I'm sorry.
This is just silly.


00:40:51.182 --> 00:40:52.672
I'm not gonna
feel A-Okay


00:40:52.750 --> 00:40:54.718
because I walked
across some damn coals.


00:40:55.319 --> 00:40:58.049
Okay, then it shouldn't be
that big of a deal, Walter.


00:40:58.155 --> 00:40:59.679
It's not a big deal.
It's just...


00:40:59.757 --> 00:41:01.247
It's a step.


00:41:01.325 --> 00:41:03.293
It's an important step.


00:41:04.094 --> 00:41:07.427
Well, it has nothing
to do with my Stephen.


00:41:07.498 --> 00:41:10.365
Walter, would Stephen
want you like this?


00:41:11.502 --> 00:41:15.063
Or would he want you to move on,
to take a step forward?


00:41:17.441 --> 00:41:19.841
You don't know
anything about my son.


00:41:19.910 --> 00:41:21.537
Walter, watch.


00:41:34.124 --> 00:41:35.853
Walter, come on.


00:41:44.702 --> 00:41:47.102
Come on, Walter.
You can do this.


00:41:50.241 --> 00:41:51.606
Come on.


00:41:52.810 --> 00:41:54.175
Walter!


00:41:59.817 --> 00:42:02.786
Okay. All right,
we all go at our own pace.


00:42:03.621 --> 00:42:05.282
He'll get there.


00:42:06.323 --> 00:42:08.188
All right, well, let's give ourselves
a round of applause


00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:13.220
For daring to kick fear
right where it hurts.


00:42:17.001 --> 00:42:20.300
Buddy, this stuff
is gonna hurt.


00:42:26.010 --> 00:42:27.978
How many layers of skin
do you think you have?


00:42:29.680 --> 00:42:31.204
Not enough.


00:42:33.684 --> 00:42:36.915
You know, you can't
do the work for them.


00:42:37.855 --> 00:42:38.913
You know that, right?


00:42:38.989 --> 00:42:40.422
The guy needs help.


00:42:41.659 --> 00:42:43.854
Fine, but you can't
do it for them.


00:42:45.095 --> 00:42:46.494
This is gonna
sting a little bit.


00:42:48.299 --> 00:42:49.527
Ready?


00:42:51.502 --> 00:42:53.094
Count of three.


00:42:53.804 --> 00:42:54.828
One.


00:42:56.240 --> 00:42:58.504
Lane! You're fired!


00:43:02.046 --> 00:43:05.345
Once you sign with us, you're no longer
an independent contractor.


00:43:05.416 --> 00:43:09.182
You've got all 32 divisions
funneling your image 24-7.


00:43:09.253 --> 00:43:13.622
Within a year, we'll increase
your household name recognition by 65%.


00:43:13.691 --> 00:43:17.252
The Burke Ryan Show will subsequently
launch in the third quarter.


00:43:17.328 --> 00:43:19.592
Followed by the DVD line,
a new set of books,


00:43:19.663 --> 00:43:21.961
syndicated
talk radio, et cetera.


00:43:22.132 --> 00:43:23.258
"Et cetera" is good.


00:43:23.334 --> 00:43:26.462
All of this lays the foundation
for a branding strategy


00:43:26.537 --> 00:43:29.438
that taps into demographics
well beyond your current base.


00:43:29.506 --> 00:43:32.441
Studies indicate that persons grieving
the loss of a loved one


00:43:32.509 --> 00:43:35.967
put on 30 to 40% more weight than
the national average.


00:43:36.046 --> 00:43:40.346
Introducing the Burke Ryan
Calorie Reduction Plan.


00:43:41.485 --> 00:43:45.046
"Finally, a loss you
can feel good about."


00:43:45.155 --> 00:43:46.349
Ooh.


00:43:47.324 --> 00:43:49.849
Look at that.
I like that picture.


00:43:51.629 --> 00:43:53.961
Wow. Are you kidding me?


00:43:55.733 --> 00:43:57.030
You look strong,
you look happy and...


00:43:57.101 --> 00:43:58.159
Right.


00:43:58.235 --> 00:44:01.170
It's a mock-up at this point.
Anyway, continuing on...


00:44:29.900 --> 00:44:31.663
LANE: Hey, that was great.
Don't forget,


00:44:31.735 --> 00:44:33.862
when Mr. Vernon
gets into town...


00:44:33.937 --> 00:44:35.700
Hey, I gotta take them
down to the museum


00:44:35.773 --> 00:44:37.968
and show them
around like an idiot...


00:44:38.542 --> 00:44:43.411
Did that beep?
Hey, Burke.
It's me, Eloise.


00:44:47.117 --> 00:44:48.675
So, where are we going?


00:44:48.819 --> 00:44:50.377
ELOISE: It's all good.
You'll see.


00:45:01.298 --> 00:45:04.358
Okay, I will be right back.


00:45:05.202 --> 00:45:06.897
Is this...
Is this your house?


00:45:06.970 --> 00:45:08.232
No, it's my mom's.


00:45:08.305 --> 00:45:10.773
I'm just gonna
go grab something.


00:45:11.775 --> 00:45:13.242
I mean, you're more than welcome
to come in.


00:45:13.310 --> 00:45:14.572
Okay.


00:45:16.046 --> 00:45:17.206
Okay.


00:45:18.982 --> 00:45:20.040
ELOISE: Hi, Mom.


00:45:20.117 --> 00:45:21.448
Oh. Hi, honey.


00:45:21.618 --> 00:45:23.142
Bob left the keys
on the counter.


00:45:23.220 --> 00:45:24.710
Oh, great.


00:45:25.789 --> 00:45:27.484
Great. How was your day?


00:45:27.558 --> 00:45:30.186
Oh, fine. I had
lots of coupons.


00:45:30.260 --> 00:45:32.751
Oh, really?
So, that was busy, huh?


00:45:33.130 --> 00:45:34.119
Mmm-hmm.


00:45:35.199 --> 00:45:37.667
Hi. I brought you flowers.


00:45:37.735 --> 00:45:40.203
Oh. Those are
so pretty. Thanks.


00:45:41.205 --> 00:45:44.299
Mom, I'd like you
to meet a friend of mine.


00:45:44.374 --> 00:45:46.535
I wasn't expecting company.


00:45:47.511 --> 00:45:50.139
Hi. I'm Burke.


00:45:51.248 --> 00:45:52.840
Burke Ryan!


00:45:53.917 --> 00:45:56.215
Ellie, you didn't tell me
you were dating a celebrity.


00:45:56.286 --> 00:45:58.277
Well, we're not dating.


00:45:58.889 --> 00:46:00.652
I wish you would have told me.
I look like hell.


00:46:00.724 --> 00:46:02.954
Not at all.
It's just the opposite.


00:46:03.026 --> 00:46:05.153
I see where Eloise
gets her looks.


00:46:07.364 --> 00:46:08.729
Let's show him
your pictures.


00:46:08.799 --> 00:46:09.823
You know,
no, I don't think so...


00:46:09.900 --> 00:46:10.889
I'd love to.


00:46:10.968 --> 00:46:12.492
No, really.


00:46:14.071 --> 00:46:16.938
You know... Okay,
I'm gonna get the keys.


00:46:17.007 --> 00:46:19.373
My word, you have
Pocahontas here.


00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:22.469
Eloise was state
archery champion
two years in a row.


00:46:22.546 --> 00:46:24.036
No.
Oh, Mother.


00:46:24.114 --> 00:46:26.981
Don't be modest.
This is Burke Ryan.


00:46:28.919 --> 00:46:31.251
(SOFTLY) I loved you
on The Today Show.


00:46:32.289 --> 00:46:33.756
Now how old is she here?


00:46:33.824 --> 00:46:35.849
Okay. I got those keys,
so thank you for that.


00:46:35.926 --> 00:46:37.860
We gotta go. Look how cute
you are here.


00:46:37.928 --> 00:46:39.953
A-Okay.
A-Okay.


00:46:40.297 --> 00:46:41.924
It was very nice meeting you.
Nice to meet you.


00:46:41.999 --> 00:46:44.524
Hope to see you again.
Yeah. Take care. Bye-bye.


00:46:45.903 --> 00:46:47.996
I am so glad you're not dating
that musician.


00:46:48.071 --> 00:46:49.436
Mother. Oh, God.


00:46:54.344 --> 00:46:56.437
I love you.
Thanks. Thank Bob.


00:46:58.182 --> 00:47:00.275
Burke Ryan.
Oh, my God!


00:47:01.585 --> 00:47:03.109
Wow.
She's so sweet.


00:47:03.187 --> 00:47:04.484
She loves you.


00:47:04.555 --> 00:47:05.715
I really enjoyed that.


00:47:05.789 --> 00:47:07.347
It was very sweet.


00:47:09.393 --> 00:47:13.022
Oh, Mom. No, no, no.
This way. Come on.


00:47:14.064 --> 00:47:15.691
Where are we going?


00:47:16.633 --> 00:47:18.123
It's fun not knowing,
isn't it?


00:47:18.202 --> 00:47:19.191
Ah.


00:47:19.303 --> 00:47:20.998
You'll see.


00:47:23.407 --> 00:47:25.671
What, are you trying
to avoid the FBI?


00:47:25.742 --> 00:47:28.836
You'll see. Please,
just get in the truck.


00:47:35.986 --> 00:47:37.317
I think I forgot
my hard hat.


00:47:37.387 --> 00:47:39.787
Oh, really?
Well, here you go.


00:47:59.509 --> 00:48:01.204
What you doing?


00:48:01.812 --> 00:48:04.144
Your chariot awaits.


00:48:05.616 --> 00:48:07.982
Seriously?
Me, in bucket?


00:48:08.685 --> 00:48:10.619
Yes. Trust me.


00:48:14.892 --> 00:48:17.656
Have you had any
cold medicine today?


00:48:17.728 --> 00:48:19.286
Not today.


00:48:19.363 --> 00:48:20.853
We're good.
Okay, now watch this.


00:48:20.931 --> 00:48:22.523
Very dangerous.
Fingers.
Uh-huh.


00:48:22.599 --> 00:48:24.931
Lock us in. Got it?


00:48:25.002 --> 00:48:26.196
Do you know
what you're doing?
Uh-huh.


00:48:26.270 --> 00:48:27.362
Ready?
Oh, Lord.


00:48:27.437 --> 00:48:28.665
Are we in? Buckled?


00:48:28.739 --> 00:48:30.229
Locked? Loaded?
Okay.


00:48:31.942 --> 00:48:35.639
All right, here lies
Burke Ryan, dead...


00:48:36.580 --> 00:48:40.573
Oh, stop it. I had a crash course
this morning from Bob.


00:48:40.651 --> 00:48:43.085
Who is Bob, and why is
my life in his hands?


00:48:43.153 --> 00:48:45.280
Bob's my mom's neighbor.


00:48:45.355 --> 00:48:47.550
Current boyfriend
of the moment.


00:48:47.624 --> 00:48:49.114
Mmm-hmm.


00:48:49.760 --> 00:48:51.625
Okay. Here's
what I was thinking.


00:48:51.762 --> 00:48:53.662
I wanted to pick up
from last night.


00:48:54.865 --> 00:48:57.356
And I wanted to get you tickets
to Rogue Wave,


00:48:57.434 --> 00:49:00.062
but they've been
sold out for weeks.


00:49:01.204 --> 00:49:05.698
So, I figured where there is a will,
there is a way.


00:49:21.525 --> 00:49:24.119
Heaven is a switchboard
that you want to fight


00:49:24.194 --> 00:49:26.458
She would even miss you
if you taught her sight


00:49:26.530 --> 00:49:28.794
Power politician
leaning to the right


00:49:28.865 --> 00:49:32.733
Baby's got a trust fund
that she'll want to go off
like that


00:49:32.803 --> 00:49:35.203
Get off my stack


00:49:35.272 --> 00:49:37.035
Leave a little window


00:49:37.107 --> 00:49:40.042
Get off of my stack


00:49:47.851 --> 00:49:49.751
Now we wear
same-colored yellow uniforms


00:49:49.820 --> 00:49:51.082
Sky is burning
but at least we're warm


00:50:00.497 --> 00:50:02.590
If I had a nickel for every time
I saw a concert


00:50:02.666 --> 00:50:04.998
from a telephone truck,
I'd be...


00:50:05.969 --> 00:50:08.199
Thank you.
It was exquisite.


00:50:08.271 --> 00:50:10.102
Don't thank me.
Thank Bob.


00:50:10.173 --> 00:50:11.606
Thank you, Bob.


00:50:12.442 --> 00:50:14.342
Hey, I got your book.


00:50:14.411 --> 00:50:15.400
I'm halfway through it.


00:50:15.479 --> 00:50:16.605
Really?


00:50:17.247 --> 00:50:19.909
Well, wait till you get
to the recipe chapters.


00:50:19.983 --> 00:50:21.780
They're top-notch.


00:50:25.455 --> 00:50:27.548
I'm sorry
about your wife.


00:50:29.192 --> 00:50:31.854
How come you didn't tell me
that's what happened?


00:50:34.164 --> 00:50:36.428
I don't know.
Never came up.


00:50:39.102 --> 00:50:41.593
Well, it sounded like
you really loved her.


00:50:43.340 --> 00:50:44.830
Yeah, I did.


00:50:46.710 --> 00:50:48.268
But that was
a long time ago.


00:50:49.646 --> 00:50:51.136
Three years?


00:50:51.848 --> 00:50:53.645
Twenty-one in dog years.


00:50:58.221 --> 00:51:01.952
I had a really,
really great time.


00:51:02.859 --> 00:51:05.054
Me, too.
That was really fun.


00:51:19.176 --> 00:51:20.473
What?


00:51:20.877 --> 00:51:24.779
I'm waiting to watch you strut back
to your bitchin' rig.


00:51:28.785 --> 00:51:30.116
All right.


00:51:31.555 --> 00:51:32.544
Bye.
